  <section|Exact source correspondence><label|exact-source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Mathematical
  content>>|<cell|<strong|Exact Lean declarations>>|<cell|<strong|Inspected
  source and role>>>|<row|<cell|Price and ticket
  variables>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.priceCore, ticketPsi,
  retractPsi, Sizing, Steady, steady_pass>|<cell|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/CoreBudget.lean.
  Here ticketPsi = ticket (TypeFace 2) (psiBudget z / L^2) and Sizing is 2 *
  card(ColorIndex) * ticketPsi \<less\>= 1/4096. steady_pass constructs
  Steady eventually in x, uniformly over the stated beta and beta-prime
  bands, including the color-count torque bound and relative-coupling bill.
  Manuscript P0 is ticketPsi; its retraction cost is
  retractPsi.>>|<row|<cell|Linearized row
  read>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.pointing>|<cell|Same
  CoreBudget.lean. It compares the linearized coarse plaquette curvature
  array with its nonlinear curvature array and compares the fine face-curl
  row with the shorter coarse row using exact_short_price, high_rows,
  support_rows, and adjust_rows. The two arrays are respectively
  flatten(dColor(1,v)) and flatten(look(spine(V,o))); their difference is a
  deterministic chart Taylor remainder. The conclusion is a phase/2048 curl
  bound and normalized parent-forecast discrepancy at most x^(-1/16). The
  parent forecast is purseMean for the same base site, coarse field, and
  beta-prime; tested patches restrict addresses but do not alter that
  forecast. The linearized curvature bound is global on every tested coarse
  coordinate; only the linear-minus-nonlinear second-order estimate is
  restricted to the support of the parent row.>>|<row|<cell|Chart and
  curvature prices>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Enlightened,
  edgeFire, illuminates>|<cell|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Illumined.lean.
  illuminates supplies chart clearance, the uniform books room bound,
  near-identity link bound, four-face heat inequality, and helm gauge/read
  error, eventually uniformly in the beta band. The manuscript keeps three
  prices distinct: priceCore for the coarse response chart, highPrice for
  each exponential-chart link, and a fixed curvature Taylor price A_* at
  least arcPrice. It uses R=x^(-3/8), t=phase(betaF), and e=(A_* + color
  dimension) R^2, and requires eventual heat/transport inequalities after
  these constants are fixed.>>|<row|<cell|Curvature
  coordinate>|<cell|YM.Gauge.curvature>|<cell|Lean/YM/Gauge/Colors.lean. The
  article writes the source curvature as the normalized real-linear color
  projection of one half the antisymmetric matrix part, in a fixed unitary
  matrix representation viewed over the reals. For group elements the source
  identity <verbatim|Ray.direct> also writes curvature as the projection of
  <verbatim|M(U)-I>. The two-factor defect is therefore the projection of
  <verbatim|(M(U)-I)(M(V)-I)> and has bound <verbatim|colorScale * chord(U) *
  chord(V)> by Frobenius submultiplicativity and the normalized projection
  norm. Iterating over four oriented links gives the exact <verbatim|1+2+3=6>
  coefficient; this is the source <verbatim|Tapes.weave>/<verbatim|warp4>
  route, not a generic four-variable Taylor assertion.>>|<row|<cell|Four-bond
  product and same-gauge transport>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.checkingMask,
  throughout, laminate>|<cell|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Rail.lean.
  laminate consumes Steady, Enlightened, StrongScope, Pose, one forest and
  one RoomView. slide_link compares the group curvature coordinate of each
  actual bond to the packaged link direction at that bond, with link chord
  and fluctuation bounds; this packaged value is not a face boundary sum.
  checkingMask takes the alternating four-link face curl, uses warp4 plus the
  four bond residuals, then applies the curvature lower bound to prove the
  healthy-face threshold. throughout gives the common-gauge corner read from
  the same purseMean, plus transported Gaussian curl.>>|<row|<cell|Same-pose
  Gaussian comparison>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.StrongScope,
  YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.laminate>|<cell|Focusing.lean and
  Rail.lean. This comparison is not reproved here. Its actual source producer
  is YM.PhysicalNext.WeightedGaussianMarginal45C.Venue.aperture with the
  LocalGaussianLaws quote/lift/remote-chip/head-switch chain, recorded in
  package A of the closure audit. This unit assumes the resulting StrongScope
  and same-pose estimates.>>|<row|<cell|Room dimension and guard
  purchase>|<cell|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.parasolPrice, ShadePay,
  tent_crowd, buys_shade, shade_auth>|<cell|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Awning.lean.
  The radius-(w*walls(y)+8) room has at most C_w (log y)^16 real link-color
  coordinates. buys_shade pays ShadePay; shade_auth transfers the paid bound
  through the actual positive-definite palette Gaussian law to Guarded and
  its away-mask probability. The manuscript's elementary coordinate argument
  is for the actual vector veil: a bond norm at least v forces a scalar color
  coordinate to exceed v/sqrt(n_G). It groups coordinates by bond, uses the
  resulting factor n_G in the reservation, and yields arbitrary fixed power
  loss from the stated hot scale without independence.>>>>>

  <section|Correlated Gaussian reserve calculation><label|correlated-gaussian-reserve-calculation>

  The source reservation in YM.PhysicalNext.PhysicalGuard7f546.Curved is
  reservation(K,U)=1/[8(1+K U)], and reserve_away proves the exact
  vector-valued away estimate used by shade_auth. The manuscript separately
  derives a slightly weaker coordinate estimate, adequate for arbitrary fixed
  power loss. It correctly uses the source cheque base price
  psiBudget(z)/L^2, while P0 is the TypeFace(2)-weighted ticket
  6*psiBudget(z)/L^2; TypeFace(2) is the six two-axis subsets of the four
  coordinate axes. The separate factor 2 in the sizing bound comes from the
  source scale inequality tau\<leqslant\>2t. These are distinct from the
  retraction base fee in retractPsi. For a centered Gaussian vector of
  dimension m whose covariance entries have modulus at most U, with
  U\<gtr\>=1, every scalar marginal variance is at most U. Chernoff's bound
  and a union bound give

  <\verbatim-code>
    Pr(max_i \|X_i\| \<gtr\>= v) \<less\>= 2m exp(-v^2/(2U)).
  </verbatim-code>

  For the actual vector veil on n_G-dimensional color vectors, an away event
  at norm v implies a coordinate event at v/sqrt(n_G). Thus its probability
  is at most 2m exp(-v^2/(2 n_G U)). Put rho=1/[8 n_G(1+mU)]; then
  1/(2n_GU)-rho \<gtr\>= 3/(8n_GU). If m \<less\>= C(log y)^16 and v \<gtr\>=
  delta exp((log log y)^(3/2)), then 3v^2/(8n_GU)-log(2m) tends to infinity.
  Therefore, eventually,

  <\verbatim-code>
    Pr(max_b \|\|X_b\|\| \<gtr\>= v) \<less\>= exp(2) exp(-rho v^2).
  </verbatim-code>

  For each fixed p\<gtr\>=0 the same growth comparison gives rho v^2 \<gtr\>=
  (2+p) log y; with y=x+c_L and x large this is at most x^(-p). The actual
  radial product veil satisfies 0 \<less\>= 1-Gamma \<less\>= 1_{max_b
  \|\|X_b\|\|\<gtr\>=v} because it is one below the half-threshold, proving
  the expected mask-loss bound for the actual correlated law. This weaker
  power conclusion alone is not the exact ShadePay field; the source's
  stronger reservation is supplied by reserve_away and the purchased ShadePay
  input.

  <section|Hypotheses retained rather than proved
  here><label|hypotheses-retained-rather-than-proved-here>

  <\enumerate>
    <item>StrongScope: actual same-pose mean/covariance bounds, positive
    covariance, palette-entry bound U, and the exact common room/forest data.
    This is package A's input/output and must hold for the same posed field
    and same finite reader.

    <item>Pose, Steady, and Enlightened, including Sizing, ticket bill,
    sufficient-row estimates, support/separation bounds, room fit, and
    health-threshold conventions. Their upstream paid histories are not
    reproved here.

    <item>Local chart and finite-product estimates: direct second-order
    Taylor bounds for the group curvature coordinate of two-link and
    four-link products, the compact-group quadratic lower bound,
    one-plaquette O(R^2) replacement remainder, and the explicitly expanded
    nautical gauge-transport bound. The constants are fixed and repurchased
    before the scale threshold.

    <item>Local window fits: the enlarged room lies inside the selected
    coarse/fine domains and every tested two-step neighborhood is readable.
  </enumerate>

  Uniformity in period is only after these fixed data and the scalar
  threshold are fixed. The conclusions are the posed laminate-type local
  estimate and this reader's own shade_auth mask payment. They do not
  establish Opacity/Acreage.Pupil, which quantifies over every matched
  palette with its Pours bound and zero socket conclusion; one actual-reader
  bound has a different quantifier.

